{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health","id":956217,"title":"Mind and Mental Health","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-23T02:11:00-07:00","id":956217,"title":"Mind and Mental Health","content":"I'm trying to do a Legacy that's about understanding your true self and contemplation, but I didn't see much in the way of that sort of thing in the 2e book. Can anyone point me at some spells that would be good to use on yourself to represent increased self awareness, understanding, and a healthier mental landscape of acceptance? I'm planning to grab the Increased mental attributes one, but I didn't really see much in the 1 and 2 dot range that seemed appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:18:13-07:00","id":956221,"title":"","content":"You could use Conditions to represent those states of mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:07:49-07:00","id":956233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health#post956217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to do a Legacy that's about understanding your true self and contemplation, but I didn't see much in the way of that sort of thing in the 2e book. Can anyone point me at some spells that would be good to use on yourself to represent increased self awareness, understanding, and a healthier mental landscape of acceptance? I'm planning to grab the Increased mental attributes one, but I didn't really see much in the 1 and 2 dot range that seemed appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Brilliant, there's an entire world-space specific to Mages that does what you're talking about -- the Astral Planes; particularly the Oneiros. The Oneiros is the landscape of the self, encompassing not only the soul, but the mind itself. It allows the Mage to interact directly with their own deepest urges and psychoses, and thereby to exorcise those proverbial demons.<br /> <br /> The problem is, of course, that Mages are hubristic. The Clavicularii and Bene Ashmedai are the two groups best known for dealing with the demons and daemons of the soul, although each takes a divergent route to that sort of self-mastery. The Clavicularii discipline the self, bringing to heel those urges they feel corrupt their clarity of vision. They bring forth their inner demons, combat and subdue them, and then utilize them as powerful tools for their Craft. They're left, at their ultimate pre-Archmage stage, with only their Virtue and their Obsessions. They see this as the ultimate form of self-control: the denial and conquering of those parts of themselves that don't fit their vision of their Perfected Self, the Key to the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The Bene Ashmedai, by contrast (as in all things), master their flaws by making allies out of them -- indulging their supposed weaknesses in order to gain control over them through that indulgence. They submit to their urges, both base and noble alike, in order to empower those parts of themselves. They then call out those G\u00f6etic entities representative of those urges, who as they have been well-treated, so in turn look kindly upon the requests of their host.<br /> <br /> In short, the Clavicularii take their flaws and turn them into tools -- the Bene Ashmedai turn them into servants. Both Legacies are left without those base urges (as pulling forth a G\u00f6etic entity from a person's Oneiros leaves the subject without the urges those entities embody), and thus reach toward self-actualization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:54:32-07:00","id":956249,"title":"","content":"As to fitting Attainments for those Legacies, I've been doing a bit of thinking that way myself. Here's what I've come up with so far:<br /> <br /> Clavicularius<br /> Parent Path: Mastigos<br /> Parent Order: Seers of the Throne or Nameless<br /> Primary Arcanum: Mind<br /> Secondary Arcanum: Spirit<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> \u2022 - Excorcist's Eye, with the Mind \u2022 added effect of being able to apply its effects to G\u00f6etic entities. Constant effect.<br /> \u2022\u2022 - Ephemeral Shield, with Mind \u2022\u2022 added effect.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 - Clear Thoughts, except that the Mage may suppress their Vice and, if successful, regains Willpower as if it were indulged (failure means they *must* indulge the flaw and gain no benefit from doing so.)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Craft Fetish, but applies to G\u00f6etic entities.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Amorality, but applies to Vice only. If Vice is indulged whilst under effect, then Virtue is suppressed instead until normal Duration expires.<br /> <br /> Bene Ashmedai<br /> Parent Path: Mastigos<br /> Parent Order: Silver Ladder<br /> Primary Arcanum: Spirit<br /> Secondary Arcanum: Mind<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> \u2022 - Combination of Know Spirit and Mental scan that only applies to spirits/g\u00f6etic entities<br /> \u2022\u2022 - Command Spirit, applies to g\u00f6etic entities.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 - G\u00f6etic Summons. Extended version, Bene Ashmedai spends 1 Mana and always counts as being in a place where she can access her own Oneiros.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Shape Spirit applied to g\u00f6etic entities. In addition, Mage may spend Mana to increase entity's Rank on a 1:1 basis (as per the Reach effect of Bolster Spirit).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 - Psychic Genesis. Mage is no longer constrained to simple commands with his \u2022\u2022\u2022 Attainment, instead gaining loyal servant. Constant effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","user":"Raikirah","date":". 08-23-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:29:24-07:00","id":956258,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1446_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1446\" data-vbnamecard=\"1446\">Raikirah</a> , did not <b>Dave Brookeshaw</b> pointed that Clavicularius will be from Silver Ladder and Bene Ashmedai from Seers of Throne?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T05:17:28-07:00","id":956271,"title":"","content":"No, I didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:52:25-07:00","id":956385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health?p=956233#post956233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Brilliant, there's an entire world-space specific to Mages that does what you're talking about -- the Astral Planes; particularly the Oneiros. The Oneiros is the landscape of the self, encompassing not only the soul, but the mind itself. It allows the Mage to interact directly with their own deepest urges and psychoses, and thereby to exorcise those proverbial demons.<br /> <br /> The problem is, of course, that Mages are hubristic. The Clavicularii and Bene Ashmedai are the two groups best known for dealing with the demons and daemons of the soul, although each takes a divergent route to that sort of self-mastery. The Clavicularii discipline the self, bringing to heel those urges they feel corrupt their clarity of vision. They bring forth their inner demons, combat and subdue them, and then utilize them as powerful tools for their Craft. They're left, at their ultimate pre-Archmage stage, with only their Virtue and their Obsessions. They see this as the ultimate form of self-control: the denial and conquering of those parts of themselves that don't fit their vision of their Perfected Self, the Key to the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The Bene Ashmedai, by contrast (as in all things), master their flaws by making allies out of them -- indulging their supposed weaknesses in order to gain control over them through that indulgence. They submit to their urges, both base and noble alike, in order to empower those parts of themselves. They then call out those G\u00f6etic entities representative of those urges, who as they have been well-treated, so in turn look kindly upon the requests of their host.<br /> <br /> In short, the Clavicularii take their flaws and turn them into tools -- the Bene Ashmedai turn them into servants. Both Legacies are left without those base urges (as pulling forth a G\u00f6etic entity from a person's Oneiros leaves the subject without the urges those entities embody), and thus reach toward self-actualization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.... Ok, good point. However, my concept for the Legacy was less about turning your urges into servants and entities and more about self-perfection through finding out who you really are and accepting that. The secondary arcana is Life, because a perfected mind leads to a perfected body sort of thing. So, I could see Astral Travel being an appropriate attainment, but I guess I was looking for things that might either be good diagnosis tools for knowing yourself (I suppose Astral Travel is the main one here) or that might be a result of that (like increasing your mental attributes). <br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:28:40-07:00","id":956446,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, you could probably do with a <i>Knowing</i> spell to dive deeply into your mind and how it works and why and all those things. On the other hand, I'd say that increasing your mental dots represent exactly what you were talking about. A fantastic <i>Presence</i> or <i>Composure</i> come from identifying those things that would throw you off kilter and addressing them, for example. Intelligence and Wits from &quot;unclogging&quot; your mental processes allowing for smooth trains of thought, Presence and Manipulation could be the result of a deep understanding of what affects you and extrapolating it into your own actions towards others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:28:39-07:00","id":956552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health?p=956258#post956258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1446_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1446\" data-vbnamecard=\"1446\">Raikirah</a> , did not <b>Dave Brookeshaw</b> pointed that Clavicularius will be from Silver Ladder and Bene Ashmedai from Seers of Throne?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As he himself replied, no. Also, in the Legacies' blurb in 2E Core it states, &quot;The foremost two Oneiric Legacies in the modern day are the Clavicularius and the Bene Ashmedai, both predominantly Seer and Silver Ladder.&quot; To my mind at least, the ethos of the Clavicularii (with its emphasis on control and dominion over the self) fits better with the Supernal symbolism of Tyranny than does the Bene Ashmedai's liberation and indulgence of the self. Should this be the case, and the Keybearers have originated as a Seer Legacy, that would also serve to explain the general mistrust the Pentacle has for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health?p=956385#post956385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I was looking for things that might either be good diagnosis tools for knowing yourself (I suppose Astral Travel is the main one here) or that might be a result of that (like increasing your mental attributes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh. Well, in that case, might I suggest Mental Scan, Body Control, Clear Thoughts, Read the Depths w/Reach effect, and Psychic Reprogramming w/Reach effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:37:37-07:00","id":956558,"title":"","content":"Temenos is formed from the collective consciousness of humanity, the Oneiros is formed from the self contained (sub)consciousness of a single individual. As such it really is ideally suited for exploration in order to understand yourself. So, if the Oneiros is self contained, how does stuff bleed together into the Temenos? What if this Legacy believes that the Oneiros is more like a sieve, holding the big chunks of you that make you who you are but allowing all kinds of run off from you to drop into the waters of the Temenos. You could make the Legacy Oneirotic explorers who find the holes in the sieves (Not necessarily just their own) and travel through those as well as being able to plug or create them. This has multiple possible purposes, they can traverse the Oneiros and Temenos laterally more easily, but it also means they can attempt to study the flux of mental forces that flow between the Temenos and the Oneiros to see how one affects the other which addresses the question how much of you is you and how much of it is everyone else, and plugging or making enough holes in the sieve could also lead to mental terraforming of both kinds of realms so you can try to become a person who is entirely just himself with no bleed through from the Temenos or blow all the holes open and find out what sticks around inside the sieve after it's been dipped in the Temenos and drawn back out again. The 1st attainment could be something like, you look at a thing in the Oneiros and are able to identify its point of origin which right at the outset could let you know (Home-grown Oneiros stuff), this is you, that's also you but wasn't always (Washed in from the Temenos, your Oneiros has been assimilating it), that's not you but you have it stuck in here with you anyway (Washed in from the Temenos and it's not being assimilated well).<br /> <br /> Feel like I'm onto something but am having a hard time explaining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:02:06-07:00","id":956574,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I think that the Goetic Legacies like the Key-bearers or the Bene Ashmedai should use Life and Mind anyway. These Legacies are about controlling yourself by perfecting your thoughts and in <i>Awakening</i>, the two inner factors that determine your thinking is your body's biology (Life) and a part of your soul (Mind).<br /> <br /> I don't really see why would these Legacies use Spirit, as that Arcanum affects things existing outside of an individual's psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:09:14-07:00","id":956580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health?p=956574#post956574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why would these Legacies use Spirit, as that Arcanum affects things existing outside of an individual's psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embodying your Vice in a form that isn't going to be immediately subject to Dissonance is generally better served by the subtle Arcanum dealing with ephemera and the wider world. Life's relation to the semiotics of defying baser urges to gain power over them is kind of tangential compared to the subset of reality that governs a mirror-world of hungry emotional symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:27:04-07:00","id":956616,"title":"","content":"I figured it was just because Spirit could actually give your goetia even more oomph since it would allow them to have Manifestations. Plus, in 1e when those legacies were created you couldn't do goetic stuff without Spirit, and so we have a legacy for a legacy.<br /> <br /> Attainments are automatically immune to Dissonance and even Quiessence <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:09:47-07:00","id":956639,"title":"","content":"After some looking at Astral Realms, I think I've gotten the Legacy to gel a bit better. <br /> <br /> The Legacy is focused on contacting and embodying the Mage's inner Supernal Self, their Daimon. In support of that they practice various meditative techniques and go on astral journeys. Some Free Council members use various modern psychological methods to attain a similar result. <br /> <br /> Oblations would be meditation, tai chi, autohypnosis, etc. <br /> <br /> Required skills would be Occult, Empathy, Academics or something.<br /> <br /> Attainments <br /> <br /> Level 1 - Mind 1, your Oblation Skill 2, Life 1(optional)<br /> Exploring the Astral and your own mind has given you insight. You may perceive the minds of others with Know Nature and, if you have Life 1 also determine their health with Analyze Life.<br /> <br /> Level 2 - Mind 2, Skill 3, Life 2 (optional)<br /> Your meditation and training have granted you the Astral Adept merit. And, if you have Life 2, you may apply the Body Control spell during your astral meditations.<br /> <br /> Level 3 - Mind 3, Skill 3, Life 3 (optional)<br /> This one should be where you start becoming one with your Daimon, but I'm not sure what that mind attainment should look like. A mind shield? Extra skills? Clear Thoughts?<br /> If you have Life 3, then, for as long as you maintain your connection with your Daimon, your appearance shifts to match it, while remaining human, per Many Faces. Your physical attributes may also shift as appropriate and you may gain one level of Striking Looks, again, as appropriate.<br /> This attainment requires a ritual to activate as the Reach would be used to get to the advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Level 4 - Mind 4, Skill 4, Life 4 (optional)<br /> Your connection to your Daimon deepens and it enhances your mind and, if you have Life 4, your body. While your Daimon is inhabiting you, from the previous attainment, you may distribute 4 points between two mental or social attributes, increasing them to the cap. With Life 4, you may distribute another 4 points between your physical attributes.<br /> <br /> Level 5 - Mind 5, Skill 5, Life 5 (optional)<br /> Again, not sure what the mind attainment should be here, but it should signify that you've seriously merged with your Daimon. So it should be cool.<br /> With Life 5 you will heal faster, even healing lost body parts over time and, if you keep the attainment up, you'll age a little slower.<br /> <br /> Reactions? Did I get this wrong anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:50:32-07:00","id":956685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956217-mind-and-mental-health?p=956616#post956616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attainments are automatically immune to Dissonance and even Quiessence <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells, however, are not, and those are the basis of goetic embodiment and by extension the Legacies' orthodox specialties, which are not, in fact, about self-control and the perfection of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}